1:1-1 (* EXPECT-ERROR: it cannot be assigned inside the loop *)
2:1-12 (* A first-match search ended by moving its FOR variable past the end,\n   `j := LEN (vars)', in zarrm9's Croissant.Build.  Up to 0.24 the loop\n   stepped and then tested, so the next test failed and the loop ended.\n   0.25's overflow-safe exit test (decision 55) holds only while the\n   variable is at or below the bound, so the loop went on and read\n   vars[4] of three.  Three of the zarrm9 gate's 53 guide documents\n   failed, and the shape below ran forever.  zarrm9's port to 0.25.0\n   observed it 2026-10-25.  The meaning of the program had moved with\n   the generator; the rule that the loop alone writes its variable (par\n   2.1) does not move.  A found flag, or a WHILE, says the same thing\n   honestly. *)
comments=2
